<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Perinthus</h1><p class="st-meta">602 BCE – 46 CE (approx.) · capital Perinthus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Samian colony on the Sea of Marmara that, with Byzantium, defeated Philip II's siege of 340 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Colonists from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/samos">Samos</a> founded Perinthus c. 602 BCE on a promontory on the north shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Propontis</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. They soon fought off attacks by Megarian settlers from neighbouring colonies.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Perinthus traded with the Thracian interior and along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Propontis</a> route to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>. It resisted the Persian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/megabazus">Megabazus</a> c. 512 BCE but was conquered. Later it paid tribute in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a>. In 340 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II</a> besieged the city with towers and rams, but Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satraps</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> helped it hold out.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Perinthus kept its independence under Hellenistic kings and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/odrysian-kingdom">Odrysian Kingdom</a>'s influence. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> a province in 46 CE, it became the provincial capital, later renamed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/heraclea-lucania">Heraclea</a>; it is modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marmara-ereglisi">Marmara Ereğlisi</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 602 BCE – 46 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58